#edb/ref 1071 "Given $X∼\\text{Po}(7),$ compute $P(X=3),$ rounded to $4$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186670463 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8cab3f8-2d4f-5187-b7bf-4e4ac59dbfe4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186670463 #edb/ref 1074 "If $X∼\\text{Po}(\\lambda ),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Po}(7),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{7}^{x}{e}^{-7}}{x!}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{7}^{3}{e}^{-7}}{3!} \\\\  & ≈0.0521.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
